{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     navbar/github-star — star the repo.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     HARD-CODED, and deliberately so. This is not the site owner's preference
     to set — it is THIS theme's own source repository, the same way a theme's
     licence or author is fixed in package.json. A custom setting for it would
     put a field in every installer's admin panel for a value only one person
     can meaningfully change.

     .ns-navicon, not NSDS's .ns-navstar: the archetype's version is a bordered
     pill carrying a live star count, and a count in markup is stale the moment
     it is written — the only ways to keep it honest are a build step or a
     fetch to GitHub on every page load. The link makes the same point and
     cannot be wrong.

     Icon-only, so aria-label carries the name the text would have.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<a class="ns-navicon" href="https://github.com/imswarnil/Namaste-Salesforce"
   rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-label="{{t "Star this theme on GitHub"}}">
    {{> "icons/brand-github"}}
</a>
